						id: "minecraft:written_book"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"{\"text\":\"The Dragonforge is used to make corresponding Dragonsteel ingots of its type using bottles of dragon blood and iron ingots.\\n\\n\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"A stage 3+ dragon, when near a fully complete Dragonforge will automatically breathe its corresponding breath on it and begin the process of making Dragonsteel ingots. This works with any stage 3+, dragon, including wild ones.\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\" If you use a wild dragon, it is recommended that you fasten it or trap it in a large cage made from blocks that it will not destroy, as the dragon will still be wild and aggressive.\\nDragons will still sleep at night (or day if it's a lightning dragon)\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"so it's advised to sleep through the night for max productivity (unless you're using a lightning Dragonforge). \\n\\n\"}"
								"{\"text\":\"It is important to note that a Dragonforge isn't just one craftable block, but a 3x3x3 cube of blocks. The blocks required are as follows: 1 Dragonforge Core, 1 Dragonforge Input (Dragonforge Aperture), 8 dragon bone blocks, and 17 Dragonforge bricks.\\nThese are the layers from layer 1, in the front to layer 3 in the back. \"}"
								"{\"text\":\"Once correctly constructed, you may insert iron ingots and dragon blood. (Depending in which forge you used, it will create Dragonsteel of the same type of Dragonforge you used.) \\n\\n\"}"
							]
							title: "龙之锻造炉"
							author: "GameTechBCxYT"
						}
					}
				}
			]
